 "notes": "Rows counted from the top of each page. p.72: rows 1-2 (Appendix) skipped; Ani's text runs over rows 3-9 (nine printed rows on p.72, so the brief's 'rows 3-8' ends one row early; I read to the end of the page, last word 'χer' 'possesseth'). p.73 rows 1-9 read; p.74 rows 1-5 read, stopping before PLATE XIII. Hall/line: hall 1 lines 1-2 (2. before Neter-χert, p.72 r4); hall 2 line 1 from ṭua (p.72 r7), 2 from t'eṭ-f (p.72 r8), 3 from àsf (p.73 r1), 4 from per (p.73 r2), 5 from àḥ (p.73 r5); hall 3 line 1 from t'eṭ (p.73 r6), 2 from Ani (p.73 r7); hall 4 line 1 from ṭua (p.73 r9), numeral 2 falls inside Ani's name on p.74 r1 (word kept on line 1), line 2 from t'eṭ-f, 3 from āper-k[uà] (p.74 r2), 4 from maāt (p.74 r4). Overlines: p.72 r3 over t'eṭ + àn (one rule) and separately over t'eṭ-f; p.72 r7 over ṭua; p.72 r8 over àn (before Àusàr ān Ani) and over t'eṭ-f; p.73 r6 over t'eṭ-f only (not over t'eṭ àn); p.73 r9 over ṭua; p.74 r1 over àn and over t'eṭ-f. No other overlines. Hieroglyph brackets: p.72 r5 [M17 M17 A1] at the end of Ani; p.74 r1 [Y3 G1 N35 Z2 2. M17 M17 A1]. Brackets only in transliteration: ī-[à] (x3), t'eṭ-[à], [maa], reχ-k[uà], āper-k[uà]. The [maa] sign on p.73 r4 is an indistinct/odd glyph, possibly a damaged or makeshift type. The small horned ring in t'at'at is the same type as the sn-sign of sep sen / sennu."
